  "_about": "Canonical scripture normalization table for tools/build-citations.py. Vulgate (Clementine) canon and numbering are authoritative: this is a Vulgate-based edition and Quaracchi's own index locorum is Vulgate. 'order' gives canonical Vulgate book order for index display. 'abbrev' = Latin apparatus abbreviations (Quaracchi). 'body_forms' = genitive/accusative/ablative forms Bonaventure uses in the running Latin body ('Ioannis decimo octavo', 'ad Romanos primo'). 'group' marks numbered books; a body form cited without its numeral resolves to '<group>*' (unnumbered bucket) and is NEVER guessed into I or II. 'chapters' powers the QA channel (a chapter beyond the book's count is a digit-confusion candidate, per CLAUDE.md's 1/4 and 3/5 classes).",
